{
  "summary": "The current build fails the primary flow: the *Add receipt* action cannot be located on the empty dashboard. The FAB lacks an accessible label and the empty‑state button text does not match the spec, causing the automation timeout. Additionally, several design details are missing or incorrect across the screens, such as missing loading states, missing error toasts, misuse of design tokens, and insufficient focus handling. These issues break navigation, leave states unhandled, and reduce accessibility compliance.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "The FAB used to add a receipt is rendered only as an icon with no accessible label or visible text, so automation (and screen readers) cannot locate or focus it. The primary flow test times out trying to click \"Add receipt\".",
      "fix": "Create a wrapper component for the FAB that sets `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` (or the exact text from the spec) and `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`. Ensure the button is reachable via keyboard/tab navigation and includes a focus-visible outline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state uses button text \"Add first receipt\" while the primary flow expects a button labeled \"Add receipt\" (FAB). The spec requires both the empty‑state CTA and the FAB to be present and labeled correctly. The current implementation only provides the empty‑state CTA with a mismatched label and no test ID, causing the flow to miss the FAB.",
      "fix": "Add both UI elements: (1) a primary FAB with `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"`; (2) an empty‑state button with the exact label \"Add first receipt\" as defined in DESIGN.md. Provide `testID` props for both and ensure they are rendered when there is no data."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑up screen does not display the loading overlay with the exact message \"Creating account…\" and fails to disable fields. The button also lacks a focus‑visible state and uses default Paper styles instead of tokens (primary colors, radius, min‑size).",
      "fix": "Wrap the Paper `Button` in the `PrimaryButton` component, pass `loading` prop, and set overlay spinner with message \"Creating account…\". Disable inputs during loading and apply design tokens for colors, spacing, and border radius."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑in screen missing the exact loading message \"Signing you in…\" and field‑level error handling. Password field does not include a show/hide toggle, and the submit button lacks a focus‑visible outline.",
      "fix": "Use the `PrimaryButton` component with `loading` and ensure the overlay displays \"Signing you in…\". Add a password visibility toggle icon with proper `accessibilityLabel`. Implement `HelperText` for inline errors linked via `accessibilityDescribedBy`. Apply token‑based styling."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission prompt modal does not use the exact copy \"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\" and the deny path lacks the \"Choose from library\" button with proper label. The image placeholder does not have an `accessibilityLabel`.",
      "fix": "Render a `Modal` with the exact title and body copy. Add two action buttons labelled \"Allow\" and \"Deny\". On denial, show a notice with a button labelled \"Choose from library\". Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Receipt photo placeholder\"` to the placeholder view."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage entry screen missing the loading overlay with message \"Saving mileage…\" and does not disable fields during submission. The success and error toasts use generic text instead of the exact wording from the spec.",
      "fix": "Wrap the save button in `PrimaryButton` with `loading` state, display overlay spinner with \"Saving mileage…\". Use `Snackbar` to show exact success \"Mileage entry saved.\" and error \"Failed to save mileage. Please try again.\" messages."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons lack disabled state and spinner during generation. The toast after sharing uses generic text, not \"Report ready to share.\" The offline banner is never shown.",
      "fix": "Disable both Export CSV/PDF buttons while generating, show a spinner next to the active button with the correct message (\"Generating CSV…\" / \"Generating PDF…\"). On success, display a Snackbar with \"Report ready to share.\" Add a top banner that appears when the device is offline (use NetInfo) with the exact copy \"Cannot export while offline.\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button component does not apply the `primaryVariant` color on press, nor does it render a 2 px solid focus ring using the `primary` token.",
      "fix": "Update the component to style `backgroundColor: theme.colors.primary` normally, `backgroundColor: theme.colors.primaryVariant` on press, and when `focused` add `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary`. Ensure min‑height 48 px and min‑width 120 px are enforced."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Theme exports `roundness: 8` but components use hard‑coded radii (`borderRadius: 4`) in some places, violating the design token usage.",
      "fix": "Replace all hard‑coded radius values with `theme.roundness` or the appropriate token (`radius-md`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay spinner uses hard‑coded color `#000` instead of the `primary` token, and the overlay background does not use `background` token.",
      "fix": "Set overlay background to `theme.colors.background` with opacity and spinner color to `theme.colors.primary`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "API error banner text \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" is not displayed because the banner component uses a generic error message.",
      "fix": "Render a banner with the exact copy from the spec when the dashboard request fails."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner uses generic wording and does not respect the token `outline` for background or text color.",
      "fix": "When NetInfo reports offline, show a banner with the exact copy \"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\" and style it using `theme.colors.outline` and appropriate text colors."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The link \"Don’t have an account? Sign up\" is rendered as plain text without a `TextLink` component, missing the hover/underline style defined in the token set.",
      "fix": "Replace with the `TextLink` wrapper and ensure the link text matches exactly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password live‑rule helper text is not shown as the user types, violating the live validation rule list requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a live‑updating `HelperText` below the password field that shows \"12 + characters, uppercase, lowercase, number, symbol\" and updates its error state accordingly."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "score": 6,
  "summary": "The sign-in screen is functional and meets basic usability needs, but lacks polish and design sophistication expected for a premium product. It's clean and readable, but feels like a placeholder with unstyled browser defaults and no visual hierarchy or spacing that would elevate it to a polished product.",
  "findings": [
