{
  "summary": "Overall the UI passes accessibility checks and uses the design tokens for colors, spacing and typography, but there are functional gaps and several deviations from the DESIGN.md specifications. The most critical issue is the missing success toast on the mileage‑entry screen, which causes the primary flow test to fail. In addition the required Floating Action Button for adding receipts is absent, screens do not enforce the global 360 px max‑content width, and some elevation/focus styles are missing. These problems need fixing before the product can be considered polished and fully compliant with the design specifications.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The mileage entry screen does not display a toast with the exact message \"Mileage entry saved.\" after a successful save. The headless UI flow timed out waiting for this text, breaking the primary flow.",
      "fix": "After a successful POST to /mileage, trigger a Snackbar/Toast component with the exact text \"Mileage entry saved.\" using the design token colors (theme.colors.success/onSuccess). Ensure the toast is announced for screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "The spec calls for a Floating Action Button (FAB) anchored bottom‑right to add a receipt, but the current implementation uses a bottom‑tab icon (camera) and never renders a FAB.",
      "fix": "Import React‑Native‑Paper’s FAB, style it to 56 × 56 px with theme.colors.accent, position it 16 px from the right and bottom edges, and have its onPress navigate to ReceiptCaptureScreen. Optionally hide the camera tab on mobile to avoid duplicate actions."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Screen.tsx (or any screen wrapper)",
      "issue": "Screens are not wrapped in the \"Screen\" component that enforces the global max‑content width of 360 px and centers content, risking horizontal overflow on larger devices.",
      "fix": "Create/use a <Screen> wrapper that applies the style { paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg, maxWidth: 360, alignSelf: 'center' } and wrap every top‑level screen component with it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "The Appbar header does not apply the elevation defined in the design tokens (elevation 1), which is required for visual hierarchy.",
      "fix": "Add the elevation style from theme.elevation (or a shadow with elevation: 1) to the Header component’s container style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx (BottomTabNavigator)",
      "issue": "Bottom tab bar lacks the required elevation (shadow) and hides the optional caption labels (tabBarShowLabel: false), diverging from the design spec.",
      "fix": "Add elevation to tabBarStyle (e.g., ...theme.elevation.card) and set tabBarShowLabel to true, styling the label with theme.typography.labelSmall (fontSize 12) and using the secondary color for inactive tabs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Field‑level validation errors are not linked to their inputs via accessibilityDescribedBy, so screen‑reader users may not hear the error context.",
      "fix": "Assign a nativeID to each TextInput and set accessibilityDescribedBy on the corresponding HelperText component, ensuring the error message is announced."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "During the loading state the overlay only shows a spinner; the required overlay text \"Signing you in…\" is missing.",
      "fix": "Add a Text component beneath the ActivityIndicator in the loading overlay with the exact copy \"Signing you in…\" styled with theme.typography.bodyMedium."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state copy does not match the spec (e.g., missing \"Tap the + button to get started.\" or using a different CTA label).",
      "fix": "Update the EmptyState component to use title \"No data yet\", body \"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\", and primary button label \"Add first receipt\" exactly as specified."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When generating CSV or PDF the buttons are disabled but no spinner appears next to the button as required by the loading state description.",
      "fix": "Render an ActivityIndicator inside the right slot of the disabled button during generation, matching the design token spacing and colors."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible outlines are only applied to tab items; other interactive components (buttons, inputs) lack a visible 2 px solid focus ring, which is required for keyboard navigation on web.",
      "fix": "Add a focus style (borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary) that is applied when the component receives focus (onFocus/onBlur) and ensure it is visible on both native and web renders."
    }
  ]
}

